"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin Chrome 159's dashed / dotted borders on boxes whose four corner
radii differ: one closed centre-line dash pattern for the box (inset t/2, each
corner arc of radius r - t/2), started where the top-left arc ends and run
clockwise, gap fitted by SelectBestDashGap over the whole loop.
Audience: browser-engine maintainers.

Chrome 159 (arm64 headless, --force-device-scale-factor=4, --window-size=400,300):
the pins are every pixel of each box whose 4x4 device block is one colour
(frame 200x48). Anti-aliased edges are not pinned. Every radius is at least
the border width (a smaller radius joins its sides differently).
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-ROUNDED-PER-CORNER-DASH-CHROME159-001 — dashed/dotted borders with per-corner radii paint as Chrome 159 does.
"""
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_renderer.{simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_resolved_engine2d_backend}

# Box 1: 4px dashed red, radii 4/16/10/20. Box 2: 4px dotted blue, radii
# 12/4/18/8. Box 3: 6px dashed green, radii 6/18/8/12.
